<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sainte-Marie among the Hurons</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1639">1639</a>–<a href="/years/1649">1649</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sainte-Marie among the Hurons was a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> mission founded in 1639 near present-day Midland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, as the headquarters of the mission to the Wendat. It included a church, a hospital and farm buildings. After Iroquois attacks in 1649 the Jesuits burned it and withdrew; a reconstruction now stands on the site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sainte-marie-among-the-hurons.jpg" alt="Sainte-Marie among the Hurons" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: P199 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Marie_Hurons_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
